  "question": {
    "text": "A ray of light coming from the point $P(1,2)$ gets reflected from the point $Q$ on the $x$-axis and then passes through the point $R(4,3)$. If the point $S(h, k)$ is such that PQRS is a parallelogram, then $h k^2$ is equal to :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "n1oCI",
      "text": "70",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "BljFA",
      "text": "80",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "iOkAG",
      "text": "60",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AET08",
      "text": "90",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/C-K8U862gtd55d-Sz0hEzM5osr-CCQ4ksbTbEikel_k.original.fullsize.png\"><br />Image of $P$ wrt $x$-axis will be $P^{\\prime}(1,-2)$ equation of line joining $P^{\\prime} R$ will be\n$y-3=\\frac{5}{3}(x-4)$<br />Above line will meet $\\mathrm{x}$-axis at $\\mathrm{Q}$ where\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{y}=0 \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{x}=\\frac{11}{5} \\\\\n& \\therefore \\mathrm{Q}\\left(\\frac{11}{5}, 0\\right)\n\\end{aligned}$\n$\\because \\mathrm{PQRS}$ is parallelogram so their diagonals will bisects each other\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\Rightarrow \\frac{4+1}{2}=\\frac{\\frac{11}{5}+\\mathrm{h}}{2} \\& \\frac{2+3}{2}=\\frac{\\mathrm{k}+0}{2} \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{h}=\\frac{14}{5} \\& \\mathrm{k}=5 \\\\ & \\therefore \\mathrm{hk}^2=\\frac{14}{5} \\times 5^2=70\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
